# Dependency Management

This app is deployed to `libapps` with formal change management, so dependency
changes must be verified, not assumed.

## Verify every update before calling it done

- Boot the app with the new versions in **both** environments:
  `RAILS_ENV=test bundle exec rails runner 'puts Rails.version'` and the same
  with `RAILS_ENV=production`.
- Run the full `bundle exec rspec` and `bundle exec rubocop`.
- For JS runtime/dev-server packages, smoke-test the actual consumer (e.g. load
  `sockjs`/`webpack-dev-server`, or boot `bin/shakapacker-dev-server`), not just
  `yarn install`.

## Use the project's Node

- Node **24** is required (`.nvmrc`). Some packages are ESM-only and only load
  via Node >= 22.12/24 (e.g. `uuid` 14). Never validate a JS dep under an older
  Node than `.nvmrc` specifies.

## Pins and resolutions must explain themselves

- Any exact pin (Gemfile) or `resolutions` entry (package.json) needs a short
  comment saying **why** (security advisory, boot regression, peer constraint).
- Do not loosen or bump a cautioned pin without running the boot + spec checks
  above.

## Audit and record what can't be fixed

- Run `bundle exec bundler-audit` and `yarn npm audit --all --recursive`.
- When an advisory has no in-range fix (e.g. a dev-only transitive dep gated on a
  major upstream bump), note it explicitly rather than silently ignoring it.
